.TH ORO-CREDENTIALS 3 "" "Oro Runtime" "Oro Runtime API Manual"
.SH NAME
oro:credentials \- JavaScript API module
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
import * as module from 'oro:credentials'
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Explicit Android 14+ password selection. Enable `[credentials] enabled = true`. WebView Autofill, passkeys and account/server authorization remain separate.
.SH REFERENCE
.TP
\fBgetStatus()\fR
Queries support without opening a provider or reading a credential. Other platforms reject with ENOSYS.
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<PasswordSelectionStatus>\fR
.TP
\fBselectPassword(options)\fR
Opens the native provider chooser after an explicit user action. Results bind to the requesting foreground document and are never persisted or logged by this API. No remote origin is asserted; providers determine app association. It does not submit a form, save/update a password or authenticate a server. Cancellation rejects ABORT_ERR; no available credential rejects ENOENT. A provider result waits at most five seconds for the requesting Activity to resume, then revalidates document ownership and the foreground window. Cancellation, navigation, activity stop and the original deadline still apply.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIoptions\fR (PasswordSelectionOptions; optional)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<SelectedPassword>\fR
